Ours.  The build uses fork, not vfork (HasVFork NO).

Imake gives HasVFork YES to every platform that is not SystemV, and
amix.cf declares SystemV4, so xinit, xdmshell and xmh were built with
-DHAS_VFORK.  Amix's libc keeps signal()'s handlers in a table in the
process's own data (_siguhandler), which a vfork child shares with its
parent: xinit's child set SIGUSR1 to SIG_IGN before exec'ing the server,
the parent's entry became SIG_IGN too, and the server's "ready" SIGUSR1
made the parent's signal trampoline call address 1 (Bus Error).

--- a/config/cf/amix.cf
+++ b/config/cf/amix.cf
@@ -42,6 +42,10 @@
 #define HasStrcasecmp		YES
 #define HasPutenv		YES
 #define HasSecureRPC		NO
+/* fork, not vfork: libc's signal() keeps the handlers in a table in the
+ * process's own data, which a vfork child shares with its parent, so the
+ * child's signal() calls (xinit's SIGUSR1 to SIG_IGN) change the parent's */
+#define HasVFork		NO
 
 /* no wchar.h/wctype.h: Xaw uses Xlib's own wide-character helpers */
 #define XawI18nDefines		-DUSE_XWCHAR_STRING -DUSE_XMBTOWC
